      "location": "Proof, Step 3.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 3.1 says: “the sets I^+(x^-) form an open cover of K, so finitely many x_1,...,x_m∈K have K⊂⋃_i I^+(x_i).” For K={p}, no set I^+(p) contains p. Compactness selects sets based at the chosen past-shifted points x_i^-, not at points x_i∈K; the subsequent coverage by J^+(x_i) is therefore not established as written. Retaining the selected bases x_i^- repairs the step.",
